NOT a measurement: these are the latencies and slots the scheduler assumes.

== 1. Register files (AIE2GenRegisterInfo.td) ==
  cm      9  cm0..cm8
  bml     9  bml0..bml8
  bmh     9  bmh0..bmh8
  amll    9  amll0..amll8
  amlh    9  amlh0..amlh8
  amhl    9  amhl0..amhl8
  amhh    9  amhh0..amhh8
  x      12  x0..x11
  wl     12  wl0..wl11
  wh     12  wh0..wh11
  y       4  y2..y5
  1024-bit accumulators and their 512-bit halves: cm0=[bml0,bmh0], cm1=[bml1,bmh1], cm2=[bml2,bmh2], cm3=[bml3,bmh3], cm4=[bml4,bmh4], cm5=[bml5,bmh5], cm6=[bml6,bmh6], cm7=[bml7,bmh7], cm8=[bml8,bmh8]

== 2. Issue slots (AIE2Slots.td) ==
  lda_slot     "Lda"  21 encoding bits
  ldb_slot     "Ldb"  16 encoding bits
  alu_slot     "Alu"  20 encoding bits
  mv_slot      "Mv"  22 encoding bits
  st_slot      "St"  21 encoding bits
  vec_slot     "Vec"  26 encoding bits
  lng_slot     "Lng"  42 encoding bits
  nop_slot     "Nop"  1 encoding bits

== 3. Audited mnemonics: slot, itinerary, [result latency, operand read cycles...], units ==
   cycles are counted from issue = 1; the first entry is when the result is written.
