   Operand bypasses: II_VMAC's accumulator operand is VEC_Bypass (forwarded one cycle early),
   II_VMACf lists none. Delay slots are not in tablegen; section 4 reads them from `ret lr`.

== 4. Local cross-check: AIE-API snippets compiled with the installed Peano (clang -S) ==
   The bundle distance the scheduler leaves between dependent ops is its latency belief.
command: clang++ --target=aie2-none-unknown-elf -std=c++20 -O2 -D__AIE_API_AIE_ADF_HPP__=1 -I <mlir_aie>/include -S snip.cc -o snip.s (snippets: SNIPPETS in tools/peano_isa_facts.py)

[bf16_mac]  19 bundles
    0  nopb ; nopa ; nops ; nopx ; mov p3, p0; nopv
    1  vldb wl0, [p0, #0]; mov p0, p1
    2  vlda wl2, [p1, #0]; paddb [p0], #32; padds [p3], #32
    3  vlda wh0, [p3, #0]; vldb wh2, [p0, #0]
    4  vlda amhh0, [p2, #32]
    5  vlda amhl0, [p2, #0]
    6  nop
    7  nop
    8  nop
    9  mova r0, #28
   10  vmac.f bmh0, bmh0, x0, x2, r0
   11  nop
   12  nop
   13  ret lr
   14  nop    // Delay Slot 5
   15  nop    // Delay Slot 4
   16  vst amhh0, [p2, #32]    // Delay Slot 3
   17  vst amhl0, [p2, #0]    // Delay Slot 2
   18  nop    // Delay Slot 1
  distance last accumulator load -> first mac: 5 bundles
  distance last mac -> first store of its result: 6 bundles
  bundles after ret (delay slots): 5

